) s2`. Deduction of the bound using case analysis on the edit distance calculation is proceeding. Realized that the symmetry theorem allows direct translation between properties. Proof of properties (3) and (4) are directly derived from properties (1) and (2) by applying `symmetry_thm`. Properties (1) and (2) can now be proven by induction on the second sequence.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"\"/home/user/lean_project/Veribench/edit_distance.lean\"","Replacement":"\"theorem edit_distance_same_head {α : Type} [DecidableEq α] (a : α) (s1 s2 : List α) :\\n    edit_distance (a :: s1) (a :: s2) = edit_distance s1 s2 := by\\n  rw [edit_distance]\\n  simp\\n\\ntheorem edit_distance_self {α : Type} [DecidableEq α] (s : List α) :\\n    edit_distance s s = 0 := by\\n  induction s with\\n  | nil => simp [edit_distance_nil_left]\\n  | cons a s ih => rw [edit_distance_same_head, ih]\\n\\ntheorem edit_distance_eq_zero_iff {α : Type} [DecidableEq α] (s1 s2 : List α) :\\n    edit_distance s1 s2 = 0 ↔ s1 = s2 := by\\n  induction s1 generalizing s2 with\\n  | nil =>\\n    rw [edit_distance_nil_left, List.length_eq_zero_iff]\\n    exact eq_comm\\n  | cons a s1 ih =>\\n    cases s2 with\\n    | nil =>\\n      rw [edit_distance_nil_right]\\n      simp\\n    | cons b s2 =>\\n      rw [edit_distance]\\n      by_cases h : a = b\\n      · subst h\\n        simp [ih s2]\\n      · simp only [h, ↓reduceIte, List.cons.injEq, false_and, iff_false]\\n        omega\\n\\ntheorem edit_distance_symm {α : Type} [DecidableEq α] (s1 s2 : List α) :\\n    edit_distance s1 s2 = edit_distance s2 s1 := by\\n  induction s1 generalizing s2 with\\n  | nil =>\\n    rw [edit_distance_nil_left, edit_distance_nil_right]\\n  | cons a s1 ih1 =>\\n    induction s2 with\\n    | nil =>\\n      rw [edit_distance_nil_right, edit_distance_nil_left]\\n    | cons b s2 ih2 =>\\n      rw [edit_distance, edit_distance]\\n      by_cases h : a = b\\n      · subst h\\n        simp [ih1 s2]\\n      · have